# Day 1 Internship Report – Restaurant Landing Page

Today, I completed the Day 1 task of my Full Stack Development Internship by creating a responsive restaurant landing page using HTML5 and CSS3. The website includes all the required sections: Header, Hero, About, Menu, Contact, and Footer. I used semantic HTML elements to organize the content and CSS Flexbox for layout. The design is fully responsive and adapts well to desktop, tablet, and mobile screens. I also added hover effects, smooth scrolling, modern buttons, and attractive food images to improve the user interface. Throughout this task, I learned how to structure a landing page, apply responsive design techniques, and create a clean and professional user experience using only HTML and CSS. Finally, I tested the website on different screen sizes, captured screenshots, and uploaded the source code to GitHub for submission.
